### 4. Create a task (protected — userId comes from the JWT, not the body)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Buy groceries",
  "taskDescription": "Milk, eggs, bread",
  "dueDate": "2026-08-20T00:00:00.000Z",
  "startDate": "2026-08-11T00:00:00.000Z"
}

### 5. Get all tasks for the logged-in user (protected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Get all tasks WITHOUT a token -> should fail with 401 Unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks

### 7. Generate a fresh token pair for the logged-in user (protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/token
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Get your own user record by id (protected + ownership check)
# Replace :id with your own _id (found in the register/login response)
@myId = 6a7b11f6c0c89150b05196b7
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/{{myId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Try to get a DIFFERENT user's record -> should fail with 403 Forbidden
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/000000000000000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Update your own account (protected + ownership check)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/auth/{{myId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "username": "testuser-renamed"
}

### 11. Try the same routes with no token at all -> should all 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/{{myId}}

